# round 41: how to cite War Balance. Each release on warbalance.org is a git tag (round-NN); cite the tag you used.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these figures, please cite War Balance and the release (git tag round-NN) you used."
title: "War Balance: where each country's money moved since 2022, toward Ukraine or toward Russia"
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "War Balance"
url: "https://warbalance.org/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/intelligent-cream/war-balance"
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: "round-41"
date-released: "2026-10-24"
keywords:
  - Ukraine
  - Russia
  - war
  - aid to Ukraine
  - sanctions
  - trade with Russia
  - frozen assets
abstract: >-
  For every country, its support for Ukraine and how much less, or more, Russia kept from trade with it (taxes and
  profit above a normal return, not the full price), plus Russian money frozen there, against a world without the war,
  from 2022 to August 2026, as totals against one year's GDP. Every number has a likely range, a certainty
  letter, a method band and its sources.
